Revision 24 was made during the design phase and lands round-7 owner call 7 together with its ADR
half in one commit (batch S-f) - the third requirements change made under the atomic process above.
It widens FR-23's population and adds AC-54. The finding (gap B #4) is that a provider offering the
container's ROOT provider as its resolution source passes all three of the adoption probe's positive
tests: it is live, it is Microsoft-shaped, and it answers for ScopedArtefactCache. Probed against the
pinned MEDI 10.0.10 - on a container built WITHOUT ValidateScopes a Scoped service resolves from the
root and returns one instance for the life of the process, disposed by nothing, so a pipeline that
borrowed it would defeat FR-1 and FR-2 while nothing complained. Where ValidateScopes is on the same
resolution throws and the probe's existing exception outcome already declines, so the gap is silent
on exactly the hosts that have validation off.

The owner's call was to ADD THE REFERENCE TEST rather than leave the case to the ADR's residue prose,
and the finding's own premise - that the probe cannot cheaply distinguish a root provider - is wrong:
each container-backed factory is a singleton and is constructed with the root IServiceProvider, so
one reference comparison per pipeline settles it.

TWO THINGS ABOUT THE SHAPE OF THE AMENDMENT, BOTH DELIBERATE. FIRST, the obligation is stated over
OBJECT IDENTITY - "the same object as the root provider the container package holds" - and not over
"the root provider". That is what makes it satisfiable by a conforming implementation, which is the
defect shape revision 18 fixed for AC-29 and round 7 found again in AC-20. Probed: MS DI injects the
root ServiceProviderEngineScope into a singleton, and the ServiceProvider object BuildServiceProvider()
returns is a DIFFERENT object with the same resolutions - so a provider handing back the sp it was
constructed with is caught, and one handing back IHost.Services is not. The rule does not ask an
implementation to detect the second; ADR 0072's residue paragraph states it as the third part of what
